WA-2025-SB5420.summary:
Recognizing the United States Space Force as Part of the Organized Militia of the State . Space Force Guardians are added to the definition of members of the organized militia of the state.

Expanding the Definitions of Military Veterans and Service Members. The definitions used to qualify persons for particular benefits for military veterans and service members are expanded to:
• members of the USPHS Commissioned Corps and NOAA Commissioned Officer Corps are included in the following preferences for:
• protection under WSCRA;
• state-sponsored fire, police, and public employee retirement systems; and
• state and local civil service exams;
• members of the NOAA Commissioned Officer Corps are eligible for license extensions for licenses issued by the Department of Licensing;
• members of the NOAA Commissioned Officer Corps and spouses of active-duty service members and veterans are included in military veteran employment protections; and
• members of the U.S. Space Force and the NOAA Commissioned Officer Corps and their widows or widowers, spouses of active-duty service members, and spouses of honorably discharged veterans with a service-connected permanent and total disability are included in the permissive preferences allowed in private employment.

WA-2025-HB2114.summary:
A person who has a defective license plate may request a replacement license plate or plates for use on the same vehicle at no charge, if the request for replacement occurs on or before the last day of the 24th month from the date of the license plate issuance.

DOL may waive the costs for a replacement license plate or plates if the request occurs after the last day of the 24th month from the date of issuance through and including the five-year anniversary of the date of the issuance.

To qualify to be replaced free of charge, a license plate must have defects such as, but not limited to, numbers that are no longer legible, or paint that is peeling or bubbling. DOL may require the defective license plate to be turned in with the request for a replacement. A defective license plate is eligible to be replaced as a set, unless only one license plate is required by law.

DOL is not required to provide a replacement license plate if:
• the license plate has been tampered with or was damaged in a vehicle collision with another vehicle, building, or object;
• the person requesting the license plate is not the owner or the person to whom the vehicle is registered and the vehicle was registered as stolen;
• a replacement plate has already been received for the license plate within five years;
• DOL has received a submitted application to transfer the license plate to a different vehicle; or
• DOL determines there is a discrepancy between the license plate and a valid registration.

WA-2025-SB6036.summary:
DSHS may exempt certain former foster care providers from AFH licensure when certain conditions are met.

Adult Family Home Licensing Exemption for Those with a Former Foster Care License. An individual is exempt from AFH licensure when the individual:
• has had an active license to operate a foster family home in Washington for at least three years;
• provided personal care services for the former foster care youth in the individual's care for at least three years on the date the youth exited foster care;
• does not have any founded or substantiated findings by child protective services or adult protective services; and
• is not the subject of a pending adverse licensing action at the time the youth in their care exits the foster care system, and the only unrelated adults the individual provides personal care to in the home are the former foster youth or youths that lived with the individual prior to exiting foster care.

Adult Family Home Licensing Exemption for Those with a Former Child-Specific Foster Care License. An individual is exempt from AFH licensure when the individual:
• is or has previously been approved by DCYF for a child-specific license;
• does not have any founded or substantiated findings by child protective services or adult protective services; and
• is not the subject of a pending adverse licensing action at the time the youth in their care exits the foster care system, and the only unrelated adults the individual provides personal care to in the home are the former foster youth or youths for whom the individual received the child-specific license.
